From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:09:35 +0300
Subject: nv30: no texture unit rewrite when its view and sampler stay the same

Mesa's state tracker passes nv30 all its sampler views (and binds all its samplers) when any
of them changes. nv30 marked every unit dirty and dropped every unit's buffer reference, so
nv30_fragtex_validate rewrote each one: TEX_SIZE1, the eight TEX_OFFSET.. words with two
buffer relocations, TEX_FILTER_OPTIMIZATION, 13 words and two buffer references per unit,
for units that kept what they had. A lightmapped game (OpenArena) switching one of its two
textures between surfaces wrote both.

A unit is now marked only when its view or its sampler is a different object. The context
holds a reference to each bound view, so an equal pointer is the same view of the same
texture; sampler CSOs aren't deleted while bound. A unit that keeps both keeps its texture
state and its buffer references too (after a flush they are re-referenced as before). The 3D
blit marks the unit it uses, as before.

A context switch (two contexts of a process on the same channel) marked everything dirty but
validated only the units changed since the context last drew, so a context could sample the
other one's textures; with fewer units marked this would show more often. It now marks all
the context's units.

Saves 13 push buffer words and two buffer references per unchanged unit when the state
tracker rebinds textures or samplers. Changes the command stream: identical rewrites of a
unit's texture state are left out. Low risk; a hardware test would show the wrong texture or
filtering on a surface.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_fragtex.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_fragtex.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_fragtex.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_fragtex.c
@@ -157,12 +157,18 @@ nv30_fragtex_sampler_states_bind(struct pipe_context *pipe,
    struct nv30_context *nv30 = nv30_context(pipe);
    unsigned i;
 
+   /* The state tracker binds all its samplers when any changes: a unit keeping its sampler
+    * (and its view, nv30_fragtex_set_sampler_views) needs no new texture state. */
    for (i = 0; i < nr; i++) {
+      if (nv30->fragprog.samplers[i] == hwcso[i])
+         continue;
       nv30->fragprog.samplers[i] = hwcso[i];
       nv30->fragprog.dirty_samplers |= (1 << i);
    }
 
    for (; i < nv30->fragprog.num_samplers; i++) {
+      if (!nv30->fragprog.samplers[i])
+         continue;
       nv30->fragprog.samplers[i] = NULL;
       nv30->fragprog.dirty_samplers |= (1 << i);
    }
@@ -179,13 +185,20 @@ nv30_fragtex_set_sampler_views(struct pipe_context *pipe, unsigned nr,
    struct nv30_context *nv30 = nv30_context(pipe);
    unsigned i;
 
+   /* The state tracker passes all its views when any changes. A unit whose view stays the
+    * same object (it holds a reference, so the same pointer is the same view of the same
+    * texture) keeps its texture state and its buffer reference, unless its sampler changed. */
    for (i = 0; i < nr; i++) {
+      if (nv30->fragprog.textures[i] == views[i])
+         continue;
       nouveau_bufctx_reset(nv30->bufctx, BUFCTX_FRAGTEX(i));
       pipe_sampler_view_reference(&nv30->fragprog.textures[i], views[i]);
       nv30->fragprog.dirty_samplers |= (1 << i);
    }
 
    for (; i < nv30->fragprog.num_textures; i++) {
+      if (!nv30->fragprog.textures[i])
+         continue;
       nouveau_bufctx_reset(nv30->bufctx, BUFCTX_FRAGTEX(i));
       pipe_sampler_view_reference(&nv30->fragprog.textures[i], NULL);
       nv30->fragprog.dirty_samplers |= (1 << i);
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
@@ -454,6 +454,11 @@ nv30_state_context_switch(struct nv30_context *nv30)
       nv30->state.vtxfmt_nr = 0;	/* the last context to draw is gone: GPU formats unknown */
    nv30->dirty = NV30_NEW_ALL;
 
+   /* The other context left its own textures in the units: write this one's again (NEW_ALL
+    * alone validates only the units marked since this context last drew). */
+   nv30->fragprog.dirty_samplers |=
+      BITFIELD_MASK(MAX2(nv30->fragprog.num_textures, nv30->fragprog.num_samplers));
+
    if (!nv30->vertex)
       nv30->dirty &= ~(NV30_NEW_VERTEX | NV30_NEW_ARRAYS);
 
